2025-10-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T19:34:02+00:00","id":"hr1057-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-06","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-06","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"1057","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001129","district":10,"fullName":"Rep. Collins, Mike [R-GA-10]","party":"R","state":"GA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-06","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Safe Passage on Interstates Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill establishes a new federal criminal offense for the obstruction of interstate highways.</p><p>Specifically, the bill makes it unlawful to knowingly engage in a listed activity with the intent to obstruct the free, convenient, and normal use of the interstate highway. The listed activities are (1) deliberately delaying traffic, (2) standing or approaching a motor vehicle, or (3) endangering the safe movement of a motor vehicle.</p><p>A violation is subject to criminal penalties.</p><p>The bill provides an exception for any lawful activity conducted or authorized by the federal government or by a state or local government.</p>","updateDate":"2025-03-24T20:39:34Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Safe Passage on Interstates Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2025-10-15T08:05:28Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-10-15T08:05:28Z"}
